{"q":"Why is Agile useful when requirements are uncertain?","o":["It uses short cycles, working increments, feedback, and adaptation instead of assuming every detail is known at the start","It prevents customers from changing requirements","It requires a complete design before feedback","It removes the need for testing"],"a":"It uses short cycles, working increments, feedback, and adaptation instead of assuming every detail is known at the start"},
{"q":"Which is one of the four Agile Manifesto values?","o":["Individuals and interactions over processes and tools","Comprehensive documentation over working software","Following a fixed plan over responding to change","Contract negotiation over customer collaboration"],"a":"Individuals and interactions over processes and tools"},
{"q":"What does Working Software over comprehensive documentation mean?","o":["Useful documentation matters, but it should support delivery rather than replace working software or become an end in itself","Documentation should never be created","Only source code should be reviewed","Users should not see working features"],"a":"Useful documentation matters, but it should support delivery rather than replace working software or become an end in itself"},
{"q":"What does Customer Collaboration emphasize?","o":["Customers or representatives participate throughout development by clarifying needs, prioritizing work, reviewing results, and giving feedback","Customers participate only after deployment","Developers should avoid stakeholder communication","Contracts must never change"],"a":"Customers or representatives participate throughout development by clarifying needs, prioritizing work, reviewing results, and giving feedback"},
