{"q":"What is a Service Provider?","o":["The system or component that offers and operates a service","The application that only consumes a service","A user who enters a password","A service registry record"],"a":"The system or component that offers and operates a service"},
{"q":"What is a Service Consumer?","o":["A user, application, or system that uses a service","The server that implements the service","A version number","A monitoring dashboard"],"a":"A user, application, or system that uses a service"},
{"q":"What does a Service Interface define?","o":["How a consumer can use a service, including available operations and interaction expectations","The private implementation algorithm","The physical location of every developer","The license price only"],"a":"How a consumer can use a service, including available operations and interaction expectations"},
{"q":"What is a Service Contract?","o":["An agreement defining operations, inputs, outputs, data formats, rules, communication, errors, and expectations between provider and consumer","A purchase invoice","A source-code comment only","A database index"],"a":"An agreement defining operations, inputs, outputs, data formats, rules, communication, errors, and expectations between provider and consumer"},
{"q":"What is Loose Coupling?","o":["Reducing direct dependencies so that services can change or be replaced with limited impact on consumers","Making every service depend on implementation details","Removing all interfaces","Putting all code in one component"],"a":"Reducing direct dependencies so that services can change or be replaced with limited impact on consumers"},
{"q":"What is Service Reuse?","o":["Using the same service from multiple applications or clients","Copying a screen into another application","Rebuilding authentication separately for every client","Using a service only once"],"a":"Using the same service from multiple applications or clients"},
{"q":"What is Service Discovery?","o":["Finding available services and their locations, interfaces, versions, and availability","Testing a password","Deleting unused services","Writing a database query"],"a":"Finding available services and their locations, interfaces, versions, and availability"},
{"q":"What is Service Composition?","o":["Combining multiple services to perform a larger business process or capability","Replacing all services with one method","Monitoring one service only","Changing a service name"],"a":"Combining multiple services to perform a larger business process or capability"},
{"q":"What are Web Services?","o":["Services accessible over a network using web technologies and standards","Only local functions","Hardware devices without software","Documents that cannot communicate"],"a":"Services accessible over a network using web technologies and standards"},
{"q":"What is REST?","o":["Representational State Transfer, an architectural style commonly used to build web services over HTTP","A message protocol that requires XML in every case","A database language","A monitoring tool"],"a":"Representational State Transfer, an architectural style commonly used to build web services over HTTP"},
{"q":"What is SOAP?","o":["Simple Object Access Protocol, a formal message-based protocol traditionally associated with XML","A client-side layout library","A version-control system","A database partitioning method"],"a":"Simple Object Access Protocol, a formal message-based protocol traditionally associated with XML"},
