{"q":"What is Backward Compatibility?","o":["The ability of a newer service version to continue supporting older clients","The ability to delete old APIs","A service's response time","A method for encrypting data"],"a":"The ability of a newer service version to continue supporting older clients"},
{"q":"Why are Service Monitoring and Logging important?","o":["They reveal requests, response time, errors, availability, resource use, failures, and security events for operations and debugging","They replace service contracts","They prevent every failure automatically","They are only for user-interface colors"],"a":"They reveal requests, response time, errors, availability, resource use, failures, and security events for operations and debugging"},
