{"q":"What is the Error–Fault–Failure relationship?","o":["A human Error can create a Fault in software, which can produce an observed Failure during execution","A Failure always creates a human error before development","They are three names for the same event","A Fault is always a user requirement"],"a":"A human Error can create a Fault in software, which can produce an observed Failure during execution"},
{"q":"What is a Test Case?","o":["Defined steps, data, preconditions, expected results, actual results, and status for testing a function or behavior","A general project title only","A source-code branch","A deployment server"],"a":"Defined steps, data, preconditions, expected results, actual results, and status for testing a function or behavior"},
{"q":"What is a Test Scenario?","o":["A broad description of what should be tested that can contain multiple detailed test cases","A single line of executable code","A defect severity level","A version-control merge"],"a":"A broad description of what should be tested that can contain multiple detailed test cases"},
{"q":"What does Unit Testing test?","o":["A small isolated unit such as a function, method, class, or module","The entire organization","Only production infrastructure","All users at once"],"a":"A small isolated unit such as a function, method, class, or module"},
